{:edb/db-before-t 402 :edb/db-after-t 403 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533715 50 #inst "2026-10-04T18:26:07.782Z" 13194139533715 true] [17592186087782 1020 #edb/ref 17592186248006 13194139533715 true] [17592186087782 1020 #edb/ref 17592186248013 13194139533715 true] [17592186087783 1020 #edb/ref 17592186248009 13194139533715 true] [17592186087784 1020 #edb/ref 17592186248016 13194139533715 true] [17592186088128 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533715 true] [17592186088128 1145 "To find the vertical asymptotes of a rational function, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors. Then, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x.$\n\nFactoring the numerator and denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{2x}{{x}^{3}-27} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x}{{x}^{3}-{3}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x}{(x-3)({x}^{2}+3x+9)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we used the difference of cubes formula to factor the denominator.\n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we set the denominator equal to zero. This gives\n\n$$\n(x-3)({x}^{2}+3x+9)=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve the above equation using the zero product property:\n\n- Solving $(x-3)=0$ gives the solution $x=3.$\n\n- The equation ${x}^{2}+3x+9=0$ has no real solutions because the discriminant $D$ is negative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & ={b}^{2}-4ac \\\\  & ={3}^{2}-4(1)(9) \\\\  & =9-36 \\\\  & =-27.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only vertical asymptote is $x=3.$" 13194139533715 true] [17592186248006 1017 #edb/ref 17592186248007 13194139533715 true] [17592186248006 1089 "q-269990" 13194139533715 true] [17592186248006 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533715 true] [17592186248006 1100 "The vertical asymptote of $f(x)=\\frac{x+3}{{x}^{2}+x-6}$ is $x=${{field-1}}." 13194139533715 true] [17592186248006 1113 #uuid "4f76e5fd-4f42-5a2b-bb6e-329cbea38e79" 13194139533715 true] [17592186248006 1138 false 13194139533715 true] [17592186248006 1145 "To find the vertical asymptotes of a rational function, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors. Then, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x.$\n\nFactoring the denominator and canceling any common factors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{x+3}{{x}^{2}+x-6} \\\\  & =\\frac{x+3}{(x+3)(x-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{x+3}}{\\cancel{(x+3)}(x-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\nx-2=0\n$$\n\nThis gives the solution $x=2.$ \n\nTherefore, the equation of the vertical asymptote is $x=2.$" 13194139533715 true] [17592186248007 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248008 13194139533715 true] [17592186248007 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533715 true] [17592186248007 1041 "field-1" 13194139533715 true] [17592186248007 1104 #edb/ref 17592186248008 13194139533715 true] [17592186248007 1110 #uuid "b494e80d-ad80-5ac0-93b8-45b7a1db27c5" 13194139533715 true] [17592186248008 1034 "2" 13194139533715 true] [17592186248008 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533715 true] [17592186248008 1111 #uuid "5128d119-c06c-5daa-9e3b-d11bb41c4c21" 13194139533715 true] [17592186248009 1017 #edb/ref 17592186248010 13194139533715 true] [17592186248009 1089 "q-270004" 13194139533715 true] [17592186248009 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533715 true] [17592186248009 1100 "The vertical asymptote of $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}-9}{2{x}^{3}-2}$ is $x=${{field-1}}." 13194139533715 true] [17592186248009 1113 #uuid "9aa64d6e-83a2-5370-b8dd-754f74c2d8ac" 13194139533715 true] [17592186248009 1138 false 13194139533715 true] [17592186248009 1145 "To find the vertical asymptotes of a rational function, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors. Then, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x.$\n\nFactoring the numerator and denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{{x}^{2}-9}{2{x}^{3}-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}-9}{2({x}^{3}-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}-{3}^{2}}{2({x}^{3}-{1}^{3})} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x-3)(x+3)}{2(x-1)({x}^{2}+x+1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we used the difference of cubes formula to factor the denominator.\n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we set the denominator equal to zero. This gives\n\n$$\n(x-1)({x}^{2}+x+1)=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve the above equation using the zero product property:\n\n- Solving $(x-1)=0$ gives the solution $x=1.$\n\n- The equation ${x}^{2}+x+1=0$ has no real solutions because the discriminant $D$ is negative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & ={b}^{2}-4ac \\\\  & ={1}^{2}-4(1)(1) \\\\  & =1-4 \\\\  & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertical asymptote is $x=1.$" 13194139533715 true] [17592186248010 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248011 13194139533715 true] [17592186248010 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248012 13194139533715 true] [17592186248010 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533715 true] [17592186248010 1041 "field-1" 13194139533715 true] [17592186248010 1104 #edb/ref 17592186248012 13194139533715 true] [17592186248010 1110 #uuid "2dd1778a-d903-52e6-b178-078939c8c056" 13194139533715 true] [17592186248011 1034 "3" 13194139533715 true] [17592186248011 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533715 true] [17592186248011 1111 #uuid "0bf8a4b5-2e48-51ce-9fd7-b6e8f4b6c3e3" 13194139533715 true] [17592186248012 1034 "1" 13194139533715 true] [17592186248012 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533715 true] [17592186248012 1111 #uuid "68a605d8-5cbb-574b-aba6-af233cb8240e" 13194139533715 true] [17592186248013 1017 #edb/ref 17592186248014 13194139533715 true] [17592186248013 1089 "q-278535" 13194139533715 true] [17592186248013 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533715 true] [17592186248013 1100 "The vertical asymptote of $f(x)=\\frac{x-1}{(x+2)(x-1)}$ is $x=${{field-1}}." 13194139533715 true] [17592186248013 1113 #uuid "ee6e8ddb-5fef-526b-86e8-b1c6eaaae58c" 13194139533715 true] [17592186248013 1138 false 13194139533715 true] [17592186248013 1145 "To find the vertical asymptotes of a rational function, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors. Then, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x.$\n\nFactoring the numerator and denominator and canceling any common factors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{x-1}{(x+2)(x-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{x-1}}{(x+2)(\\cancel{x-1})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x+2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\nx+2=0\n$$\n\nThis gives the solution $x=-2.$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the vertical asymptote is $x=-2.$" 13194139533715 true] [17592186248014 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248015 13194139533715 true] [17592186248014 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533715 true] [17592186248014 1041 "field-1" 13194139533715 true] [17592186248014 1104 #edb/ref 17592186248015 13194139533715 true] [17592186248014 1110 #uuid "ddbf5b17-be2f-5fbe-8a10-e2627bcddc0a" 13194139533715 true] [17592186248015 1034 "-2" 13194139533715 true] [17592186248015 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533715 true] [17592186248015 1111 #uuid "18d954d3-7da1-55ef-aafc-3da0ef6c6fa1" 13194139533715 true] [17592186248016 1017 #edb/ref 17592186248017 13194139533715 true] [17592186248016 1089 "q-6913" 13194139533715 true] [17592186248016 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533715 true] [17592186248016 1100 "Find all of the vertical asymptotes of the function $f(x)=\\frac{x}{{x}^{3}+2x}.$" 13194139533715 true] [17592186248016 1113 #uuid "2d87d550-5004-5d22-b9a3-b2335e96082d" 13194139533715 true] [17592186248016 1138 false 13194139533715 true] [17592186248016 1145 "To find the vertical asymptotes of a rational function, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors. Then, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x.$\n\nFactoring the numerator and denominator and canceling any common factors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{x}{{x}^{3}+2x} \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{x({x}^{2}+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{x}}{\\cancel{x}({x}^{2}+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we set the denominator equal to zero:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+2=0\n$$\n\nThis equation does not have any real solutions. Therefore, $f(x)$ does not have any vertical asymptotes." 13194139533715 true] [17592186248017 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248018 13194139533715 true] [17592186248017 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248019 13194139533715 true] [17592186248017 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248020 13194139533715 true] [17592186248017 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248021 13194139533715 true] [17592186248017 1000 #edb/ref 17592186248022 13194139533715 true] [17592186248017 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533715 true] [17592186248017 1041 "selection" 13194139533715 true] [17592186248017 1104 #edb/ref 17592186248022 13194139533715 true] [17592186248017 1110 #uuid "42e10a13-8285-506a-bade-53788ddaf33a" 13194139533715 true] [17592186248018 1034 "x=-2,\\,x=0,\\,x=2" 13194139533715 true] [17592186248018 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533715 true] [17592186248018 1111 #uuid "9dfe1985-d4cb-5492-bd5d-9558e920c0b2" 13194139533715 true] [17592186248019 1034 "x=-\\sqrt{2},\\,x=\\sqrt{2}" 13194139533715 true] [17592186248019 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533715 true] [17592186248019 1111 #uuid "4863b7d9-e542-59d6-9d18-6b7e5cb3485a" 13194139533715 true] [17592186248020 1034 "$x=0$ only" 13194139533715 true] [17592186248020 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533715 true] [17592186248020 1111 #uuid "ea841a13-1cac-51d7-b05c-de5daabcbf75" 13194139533715 true] [17592186248021 1034 "x=-\\sqrt{2},\\,x=0,\\,x=\\sqrt{2}" 13194139533715 true] [17592186248021 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533715 true] [17592186248021 1111 #uuid "80f56930-3850-520c-9abd-ede0c6c067c9" 13194139533715 true] [17592186248022 1034 "The function has no vertical asymptotes" 13194139533715 true] [17592186248022 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533715 true] [17592186248022 1111 #uuid "fd852a2f-ac3c-5b80-9c7e-73a1924aef5e" 13194139533715 true]] :edb/tempids {"q